          }
        ],
        "author": {
          "name": "Patrick Farrell",
          "email": "patrick@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-11-24 19:59:26.000000000",
          "tz": 0
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "patrick bot",
          "email": "patrick-bot@mulberrytree.us",
          "date": "2026-11-24 19:59:26.000000000",
          "tz": 0
        },
        "subject": "LU-20157 llite: own EC pages again to discard them",
        "message": "LU-20157 llite: own EC pages again to discard them\n\nvvp_io_ec_rd_end() releases the pages an EC read recovered by\nlocking each folio by hand, deleting its cl_page and removing the\nfolio from the page cache, which open codes cl_page_discard().  The\npages were disowned for the copy to userspace, and cl_page_discard()\nneeds the page owned by the IO.\n\nOwn each page again with cl_page_own() and use the usual discard and\ndisown pair.  cl_page_own() fails on a page that a lock cancel\ndeleted during the copy, which replaces the explicit CPS_FREEING\ncheck.  Such a page is no longer reachable from its folio, so its\ncp_ec_recovery is cleared without the folio lock.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity-ec\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I5cf19cd150c22049216a5d7e9fcade963a67eec2\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master",
      "description": "Edit commit message"
    }
